  "_comment": "Concepts annotated on Figure 1B and tabulated in the SI. Each concept is written the conventional way in each language, so that a language which lexicalises it as one compound (typically German) is compared with one that spells it out as a phrase (typically English/French/Italian/Spanish). src/count_phrases.py tokenises the printed surface the SPGC way (lowercase; whitespace and apostrophes separate, so \"bouteille d'eau\" is the 3-gram bouteille/d/eau) and counts exact k-gram occurrences over the manifest books. This list is fixed BEFORE any count is looked at, and every concept in it is reported in the SI table whatever the outcome -- including the failures. SPGC is dominated by pre-1900 literature, so the concepts marked 'modern' are expected to be rare or absent; they are kept in deliberately, as a documented limitation rather than a silently dropped case.",
